# Rover P4 95 four-door saloon, 1962-1964.
#
# The 2.5-litre six P4 of the final series, with the 1962 grille and the
# last P4 body details. It sat between the 100 and the 110 in the final range.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P4
#
# Dimensions: variant-specific overall figures were not established; the
# family wheelbase is 2.819 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is a 29 GYX
# car identified by Commons as a 95; the rear view is tilted. The flank is
# estimated; the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (b), the P4 Drivers Guild's year-based compilation. Black,
# Sage Green, Dove Grey and Maroon. Weights 6, 5, 5, 4, total 20, provisional.
#
# Speed 150 km/h. Comfort 65/280, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1962 intro, retires staggered 1980-1983.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p4-95.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p4-95.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p4-95/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the wing script is not readable, the lower front marker
# lamps are incomplete, and the rear glass needs more curvature. The rear view
# in the pack is tilted and was used for fittings, not dimensions. At 128 px the
# late P4 grille and lamps read as a P4 95.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP495(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=6
intro_year=1962
intro_month=9
retire_year=1983
retire_month=6
speed=150
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=280

Image[E]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_N.0.0,0,33
Image[NE]=./images/rover-p4-95-black_NE.0.0,0,24
